{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [48.982799919999984, 40.37306509999996, 289.82858931, 97.53923689631358], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "Data sharing. The data sharing policy, including restrictions, of Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC, a subsidiary of Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA (MSD)  is available at: https://trialstransparency.msdclinicaltrials.com/ policies-perspectives.aspx.  Requests  for  access  to  the  clinical  study  data can be submitted via email to the Data Access mailbox (mailto: dataaccess@msd.com)."}, {"bbox": [48.982799919999984, 100.35311534000004, 289.84058916000004, 177.5326369663136], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "Patient consent statement. DRIVE-FORWARD, DRIVE-AHEAD, and DRIVE-SHIFT trials were conducted in conformance with International Council for Harmonisation Guidelines for Good Clinical Practice and applicable regulations regarding the protection of human participants in biomedical research. The protocols were approved by the independent ethics committee  for  each  study  site,  and  all  participants  provided  written  informed consent before any study procedures were performed. No additional data were collected for the current post hoc analysis."}, {"bbox": [48.982799919999984, 180.34651541000005, 289.79898968, 197.48838751631365], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "Financial  support. Funding  for  this  research  was  provided  by  Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC, a subsidiary of Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA."}, {"bbox": [48.982799919999984, 200.35906525000007, 289.83658921, 477.49368740631365], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "Potential conflicts of interest. K.S., Z.J.X., W.G., R.M.P., and Y.W. are current or former employees of Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC, a subsidiary of Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA, who may own stock and/or hold stock options in Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA. R.L. is an employee of MSD France, Puteaux, France, and may own stock and/or hold stock options in Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA. S.L.W. has received consulting fees from MSD, ViiV Healthcare, GSK and Gilead Sciences; honoraria from  Merck  &  Co.,  Inc.,  Rahway,  NJ,  USA,  ViiV  Healthcare,  GSK  and Gilead  Sciences;  and  research  grants  paid  to  her  institution  from  Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA, Gilead Sciences, ViiV Healthcare, Janssen and  GSK.  P.N.K.  has  received  research  grants  paid  to  her  institution from Gilead Sciences, ViiV Healthcare, GSK, Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ,  USA,  and  Theratechnologies;  received  advisory  board  fees  from Gilead  Sciences,  ViiV  Healthcare,  GSK,  and  Merck;  and  own  stock  or hold stock options in Gilead Sciences, ViiV Healthcare, GSK, Theratechnologies, Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA, Pfizer, Johnson &  Johnson,  and  Moderna.  C.O.  has  received  honoraria  from  Janssen, Gilead  Sciences,  ViiV  Healthcare,  MSD,  and  Bavarian  Nordic;  received support for attending  meetings and/or travel from  Janssen, Gilead Sciences,  ViiV  Healthcare,  MSD,  and  Bavarian  Nordic;  advisory  board fees from Janssen, Gilead Sciences, ViiV Healthcare, MSD, and Bavarian Nordic; and research grants paid to her institution from Janssen, Gilead Sciences, ViiV Healthcare, MSD, and AstraZeneca. M.T. is a member of the IAS-USA  Antiretroviral Guidelines Panel and co-chair of the HIVMA/IDSA HIV Primary Care Guidance Panel; has received personal fees  to  serve  as  Independent  Data  Monitoring  Committee  chair  from Excision Biotherapeutics; and has received research support paid to her institution from Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA."}, {"bbox": [48.982799920000005, 496.05136905, 96.08621112, 504.05126905000003], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 4, "source": "docling", "text": "References"}, {"bbox": [52.3842, 508.2871302, 289.5899224999999, 541.5968040524347], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 5, "source": "docling", "text": "Squires K, Bekker LG, Katlama C, et al. Influence of sex/gender and race on responses to raltegravir combined with tenofovir-emtricitabine in treatment-naive human  immunodeficiency  virus-1  infected  patients:  pooled  analyses  of  the STARTMRK and QDMRK studies. Open Forum Infect Dis 2017 ; 4:ofw047."}, {"bbox": [52.3842, 544.28640162, 289.55282356, 577.5967754524347], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 6, "source": "docling", "text": "Rawlings MK, Letang E, Quercia R, et al. Evaluating diversity in randomized clinical trials of dolutegravir-based antiretroviral therapy regimens: pooled 48-week analyses by race, sex, and regional subgroups. Open Forum Infect Dis 2022 ;  9: ofac304."}, {"bbox": [52.3842, 580.3423714200001, 289.60042219999997, 595.5680619724346], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 7, "source": "docling", "text": "Li N, Zheng HY, He WQ, et al. Treatment outcomes amongst older people with HIV infection receiving antiretroviral therapy. AIDS 2024 ; 38:803-12."}, {"bbox": [52.3842, 598.31435792, 289.5906224799999, 622.6103893124347], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "list_item", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 8, "seq": 8, "source": "docling", "text": "Mizuno Y, Frazier EL, Huang P, Skarbinski J. Characteristics of transgender women  living  with  HIV  receiving  medical  care  in  the  United  